    <!-- ZC-1482 (train OT213n B2): the mode intro dialog's texts. The two bodies are byte for byte MODE_INTRO_TUNNEL_BODY and MODE_INTRO_OPEN_BODY (ConversationModeUi.kt), which the honesty tests pin. -->
    <string name="chat_mode_intro_title">Choose how each chat travels</string>
    <string name="chat_mode_intro_tunnel_body">Tunnel: a secure handshake, then free messages through the same Nostr relays as Open. If you never finished a handshake with this contact, switching to Tunnel costs two or three on-chain payments, each at least 0.00017 ZEC; the exact number is shown before you pay, and both of you need ZChat 2.13 or newer.</string>
    <string name="chat_mode_intro_open_body">Free, end-to-end encrypted messages through three Nostr relays, one run by ZChat and two by other people. Relays can\'t read them. But each relay can see your chat key (one key for all your chats), your IP address, when you\'re online, and which chat keys you send to. Needs the contact\'s ZCHAT code (scan their QR or paste their zchat: link), which carries their chat key; with only a bare Zcash address, use Tunnel instead. Voice calls allowed.</string>
    <string name="chat_mode_intro_footer">All three modes are end-to-end encrypted. The mode is picked per conversation and can be changed anytime in the chat header.</string>
